# ============================================================
# .npmrc example - for consumer applications
# ============================================================
# Copy this file into the ROOT folder of your consumer project
# and rename it to ".npmrc" (remove the .example extension).
#
# NOTE: Do NOT hardcode an actual token in this file - the
# token is picked up from an environment variable
# (SOLIFI_NPM_TOKEN) at runtime.
# ============================================================

# Packages under the @solifi scope will be resolved from the GitLab Package Registry
@solifi:registry=https://gitlab.solifi.com/api/v4/groups/<GROUP_ID>/-/packages/npm/

# Auth token - picked up from an env variable, do not put the literal value here
//gitlab.solifi.com/api/v4/packages/npm/:_authToken=${SOLIFI_NPM_TOKEN}

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Setup steps (one-time, each developer does this on their own machine):
#
# 1) Replace <GROUP_ID> with your actual Solifi GitLab group ID
#    (GitLab group -> Settings -> General -> "Group ID")
#
# 2) Create your own Personal Access Token:
#    GitLab -> Profile -> Access Tokens -> scope: read_api (or read_package_registry)
#
# 3) Open a new terminal, then install the package:
#        npm install @solifi/platform-ui@1.2.5
# ------------------------------------------------------------
